  "definition": "A prostaglandin is part of a group of body chemicals made through a process regulated by the cyclooxygenase enzymes encoded by PTGS1 and PTGS2. This pathway is important because it is a major target of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs).",
